    "body": "@davidkna That was my entire _.zshrc_. That was the sole file I had related to zsh config in my home directory.\r\n\r\nTo test further I have:\r\n\r\n- Created a new user:\r\n  - install _rustup_\r\n  - install _starship_\r\n  - add `eval \"$(starship init bash)\"` to .bashrc.\r\n  - Starship behaves as expected (changes to error character)\r\n- Change new user to zsh:\r\n  - _chsh_ to _/bin/zsh_\r\n  - add `eval \"$(starship init zsh)\"` to _.zshrc_\r\n  - _rustup_ already added _.zshenv_ with  `. \"$HOME/.cargo/env\"`\r\n  - Starship does not behave as expected (no error character).\r\n\r\nCurrent files in new user folder:\r\n#### .zshrc\r\n```zsh\r\neval \"$(starship init zsh)\"\r\n```\r\n#### .zshenv\r\n```zsh\r\n. \"$HOME/.cargo/env\"\r\n```\r\n\r\n#### apt show zsh\r\n```\r\nPackage: zsh\r\nVersion: 5.3.1-4+deb9u5\r\nPriority: optional\r\nSection: shells\r\nMaintainer: Debian Zsh Maintainers <pkg-zsh-devel@lists.alioth.debian.org>\r\nInstalled-Size: 2,202 kB\r\nPre-Depends: dpkg (>= 1.17.14)\r\nDepends: zsh-common (= 5.3.1-4+deb9u5), libc6 (>= 2.15), libcap2 (>= 1:2.10), libtinfo5 (>= 6)\r\nRecommends: libc6 (>= 2.23), libncursesw5 (>= 6), libpcre3\r\nSuggests: zsh-doc\r\nHomepage: http://www.zsh.org/\r\nDownload-Size: 817 kB\r\nAPT-Manual-Installed: yes\r\nAPT-Sources: http://security.debian.org/debian-security stretch/updates/main amd64 Packages\r\n```\r\n",
